Whole-context initial-review reuse retains all three original compact observation pins, exports, launch/completion/trace, adapter/method/addendum bindings, and actual original sessions/wave. It is allowed only when the complete existing context plus declared recording method match and the entire first three reviews are complete with valid procedure, including unfavorable judgments. A changed member, source/view/provenance/method context, incomplete first record, or altered compact raw cannot be repaired by partial reuse or a critic replacement. The new preparer marks invalid initial evidence unready; it does not silently request three more critics.

Archive verification can inject `ByteAccess(reader=...)` or `ByteAccess(path_map=...)`, or use the binding audit's `--archive-map` option with an explicit JSON mapping from original absolute pins to archived files. Archive mode has no original-host fallback. Only declared packet/launch/helper/report pins use that map; unknown raw observed paths remain strings with their original uncertainty, never aliases that claim successful viewing. The binding audit certifies byte/provenance relationships only; the unchanged v4 summary and source-attestation/effective NA gates continue to decide whether the preserved viewing/assessment was usable. Replaying valid bindings for an NA raw record cannot promote its quality or viewing gate.

Deployment: run the v2 preparer and auditor directly from `ROOT/method-recording-v2`; do not copy them over ROOT helpers. Freeze this one helper chain together with runtime J and the unchanged producer/evaluation helper bytes before any R10 production. Use the same exact helper paths for both initial and selected preparation, so whole-context reuse has no phase-dependent method change. The preparer accepts literal `--wave initial` or `--wave selected` using the original `--corpus/--production/--out/--candidate-label/--initial-root` interface. For fresh reviews audit with `--packet PACKET --report-dir PHASE/cli --output NEW_AUDIT`; for strictly valid whole-context reuse use `--packet SELECTED_PACKET --reuse REUSE_JSON --output NEW_AUDIT`. Preserve the original v4 summary separately and apply its unchanged quality/procedure gates plus recording/source/effective NA validity. No real preparation, production, reviewer, image, or CLI actor is launched during metadata-only integration verification. This prospective method never exports or rewrites old R9 records.

